{
 "voAvailable": true,
 "scenes": [
  {
   "scene": 1,
   "title": "THE SECRET",
   "start": 0.55,
   "end": 7.681,
   "tempo": 1,
   "words": 21,
   "text": "Some of Egypt’s greatest pharaohs were discovered together in a secret tomb— not beneath a pyramid, but hidden in a cliff."
  },
  {
   "scene": 2,
   "title": "THE LOOTED TOMBS",
   "start": 10.55,
   "end": 18.204,
   "tempo": 1,
   "words": 19,
   "text": "Their original burial places had been threatened by thieves. Gold vanished, coffins were damaged, and royal mummies were disturbed."
  },
  {
   "scene": 3,
   "title": "A PLAN TO SAVE THE KINGS",
   "start": 20.55,
   "end": 26.637,
   "tempo": 1,
   "words": 17,
   "text": "By the Twenty-first Dynasty, priests of Amun were determined to rescue the dead rulers of earlier centuries."
  },
  {
   "scene": 4,
   "title": "REWRAPPED IN LINEN",
   "start": 30.55,
   "end": 37.185,
   "tempo": 1,
   "words": 14,
   "text": "They inspected tombs, repaired damaged burials, and carefully rewrapped royal bodies in fresh linen."
  },
  {
   "scene": 5,
   "title": "PRESERVING THEIR NAMES",
   "start": 40.55,
   "end": 47.499,
   "tempo": 1,
   "words": 19,
   "text": "Labels recorded names and transfers. Some of the mummies were moved several times before reaching their final hiding place."
  },
  {
   "scene": 6,
   "title": "THE GREAT PHARAOHS",
   "start": 50.55,
   "end": 57.368,
   "tempo": 1,
   "words": 19,
   "text": "Among them were famous rulers, including Seti the First and Ramesses the Second, whose tombs had suffered from robbery."
  },
  {
   "scene": 7,
   "title": "DEIR EL-BAHARI",
   "start": 60.55,
   "end": 68.152,
   "tempo": 1,
   "words": 19,
   "text": "Their destination was a remote place among the limestone cliffs of Deir el-Bahari, across the Nile from ancient Thebes."
  },
  {
   "scene": 8,
   "title": "TT320",
   "start": 70.55,
   "end": 78.491,
   "tempo": 1,
   "words": 21,
   "text": "The hiding place, now called TT three-twenty, was also the burial place of High Priest Pinedjem the Second and his family."
  },
  {
   "scene": 9,
   "title": "MORE THAN FIFTY",
   "start": 80.55,
   "end": 88.988,
   "tempo": 1,
   "words": 18,
   "text": "There, more than fifty people, including kings, queens, and other royal figures, rested among coffins and funerary objects."
  },
  {
   "scene": 10,
   "title": "SEALED BY TIME",
   "start": 90.55,
   "end": 97.499,
   "tempo": 1,
   "words": 18,
   "text": "Sand and fallen stones concealed the entrance. Over many generations, the location slipped from the wider world’s knowledge."
  },
  {
   "scene": 11,
   "title": "THE FAMILY",
   "start": 100.55,
   "end": 106.584,
   "tempo": 1,
   "words": 16,
   "text": "Then, in the nineteenth century, members of the local Abd el-Rassul family discovered the hidden chambers."
  },
  {
   "scene": 12,
   "title": "THE GOAT LEGEND",
   "start": 110.55,
   "end": 117.786,
   "tempo": 1,
   "words": 20,
   "text": "According to a famous but uncertain story, a wandering goat fell into a shaft, and its owner followed it below."
  },
  {
   "scene": 13,
   "title": "A CHAMBER OF KINGS",
   "start": 120.55,
   "end": 128.334,
   "tempo": 1,
   "words": 20,
   "text": "What he supposedly found was astonishing: a passage filled with royal coffins, some marked with the cobra symbols of kingship."
  },
  {
   "scene": 14,
   "title": "CLUES IN THE MARKET",
   "start": 130.55,
   "end": 139.17,
   "tempo": 1,
   "words": 19,
   "text": "Objects began circulating on the antiquities market. Their inscriptions drew suspicion, and investigators traced the trail toward the family."
  },
  {
   "scene": 15,
   "title": "1881: THE SECRET REVEALED",
   "start": 140.55,
   "end": 148.517,
   "tempo": 1,
   "words": 20,
   "text": "In eighteen eighty-one, the secret was revealed. On July sixth, Émile Brugsch and Ahmed Kamal arrived to secure the tomb."
  },
  {
   "scene": 16,
   "title": "THE RUSHED REMOVAL",
   "start": 150.55,
   "end": 158.622,
   "tempo": 1,
   "words": 20,
   "text": "The contents were cleared in roughly forty-eight hours. But poor documentation and damage during removal would trouble generations of researchers."
  },
  {
   "scene": 17,
   "title": "AN EXTRAORDINARY LEGACY",
   "start": 160.55,
   "end": 169.144,
   "tempo": 1,
   "words": 22,
   "text": "In twenty twenty-one, ten royal mummies discovered in this cache joined Egypt’s Pharaohs’ Golden Parade on their journey to a new museum."
  },
  {
   "scene": 18,
   "title": "HIDDEN, NOT FORGOTTEN",
   "start": 170.55,
   "end": 178.935,
   "tempo": 1,
   "words": 23,
   "text": "The cache preserved a lost chapter of Egyptian history: kings rescued from robbers, concealed for centuries, and finally brought back into the light."
  }
